ons","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the non-Euclidean passage — the Bank of Zork’s curtain of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"light, where the room you arrive in depends on state rather than on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the exit you took:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["depository.north { lastViewingRoom == .west ? smallRoom : vault }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Travel runs through the same path as every other passable exit, so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"onEnter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rules fire and a boarded vehicle rides along —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the difference between this and assigning "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.location"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a rule, where neither happens.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"read","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": it may run more than once in a turn — FOLLOW","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asks it which way the quarry went before travel takes it — so it must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answer from state rather than change any.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two consequences of the destination being a closure:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is not validated at bootstrap, and an invalid destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The other exit forms name a room the bootstrap can resolve;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"this one is opaque until it runs, and running it at launch would","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"prove nothing, since it may answer differently every turn. So a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination that isn’t a stored property of the game — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"built inside the closure, say — compiles and boots, and the first","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time anything asks this exit where it leads the engine stops the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game with a "},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" naming this room, this direction and the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name the returned "},{"code":"Location","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares. There is no in-game refusal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to fall back on: this is an authoring mistake, and it is as fatal in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a shipped binary as it is in a test."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"It contributes nothing to the reachable-room set","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which is built"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"from declared destinations, and nothing to the adjacency the naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reach is drawn from. A room reachable ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" this way reads to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"engine as off-map, so FOLLOW will not name somebody standing there;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and standing on this side of a dynamic exit does not make the far"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"side “next door”, so somebody over there is nameable once they have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"been met and not before. Both are the same reason — the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is code, and scope is computed on every parse rather than on every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"move. For a room the map doesn’t admit to, that is usually what you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"want; when it isn’t, declare an ordinary exit as well, from whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room you want the adjacency to hold from."}]}]}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV4exit_6towardAA8MapEntryVAA9DirectionO_ACyYbctF","title":"exit(_:toward:)","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"exit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Direction","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9DirectionO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"toward","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MapEntry","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/exit(_:toward:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The general dynamic exit: ","type":"text"},{"code":"destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is evaluated at ","type":"text"},{"code":"go","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" time, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one direction can lead to different rooms on different turns.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"ide